const C3S23_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "וַיִּהְיוּ חַיֵּי שָׂרָה מֵאָה שָׁנָה וְעֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה וְשֶׁבַע שָׁנִים שְׁנֵי חַיֵּי שָׂרָה", "en": "The lifetime of Sarah consisted of one hundred years, twenty years and seven years. [These were] the years of Sarah’s life.", "c": [["The lifetime of Sarah consisted of one hundred years, twenty years and seven years", "The reason the word שָׁנָה [year] is written with every set is to tell you that every set is to be explained by itself. [When she was] 100 years old she was like a 20 year old, regarding sin. Just as when she was 20 she was not considered as having sinned since she was not yet subject to punishment, so, too, at 100 she had not sinned. And when she was 20 she was like a seven-year-old, regarding [her] beauty.", "ויהיו חיי שרה מאה שנה ועשרים שנה ושבע שנים. לכך נכתב שנה בכל כלל וכלל, לומר לך שכל אחד נדרש לעצמו, בת ק' כבת כ' לחטא, מה בת כ' לא חטאה שהרי אינה בת עונשין, אף בת ק' בלא חטא, ובת כ' כבת ז' ליופי:"], ["The years of Sarah’s life", "[This tells us] that they were all equally good.", "שני חיי שרה. כֻּלן שוין לטובה:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתָּמָת שָׂרָה בְּקִרְיַת אַרְבַּע הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן וַיָּבֹא אַבְרָהָם לִסְפֹּד לְשָׂרָה וְלִבְכֹּתָהּ", "en": "Sarah died in Kiryas Arba, which is Chevron, in the land of Canaan. Avraham came to eulogize Sarah and to weep for her.", "c": [["In Kiryas Arba", "So called because of the four giants that were there, Achiman, Sheishai, Talmai, and their father. Another explanation: So called because of the four couples that were buried there—man and wife, Adam and Chavah, Avraham and Sarah, Yitzchok and Rivkah, Yaakov and Leah.", "בקרית ארבע. על שם ארבע ענקים שהיו שם, אחימן ששי ותלמי ואביהן. דבר אחר, על שם ארבע זוגות שנקברו שם איש ואשתו,אדם וחוה, אברהם ושרה, יצחק ורבקה, יעקב ולאה (ב\"ר נח, ד):"], ["Avraham came", "From Beer Sheva.", "ויבא אברהם. מבאר שבע:"], ["To eulogize Sarah and to weep for her", "The narrative of Sarah’s death immediately follows the Akeidah [binding] of Yitzchok because as a result of the news of the Akeidah, that her son had been prepared for slaughter and almost not been slaughtered, her soul departed from her and she died.", "לספוד לשרה ולבכתה. נסמכה מיתת שרה לעקידת יצחק, לפי שעל ידי בשורת העקידה, שנזדמן בנה לשחיטה וכמעט שלא נשחט, פרחה נשמתה ממנה ומתה:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיָּקָם אַבְרָהָם מֵעַל פְּנֵי מֵתוֹ וַיְדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי־חֵת לֵאמֹר", "en": "Avraham rose from the presence of his dead, and spoke to the sons of Cheis saying,", "c": []}], [{"he": "גֵּר־וְתוֹשָׁב אָנֹכִי עִמָּכֶם תְּנוּ לִי אֲחֻזַּת־קֶבֶר עִמָּכֶם וְאֶקְבְּרָה מֵתִי מִלְּפָנָי", "en": "I am a foreigner and a resident among you. Grant me the possession of a grave site with you, so that I may bury my dead from my presence.", "c": [["I am a foreigner and a resident among you", "“A stranger from another land and I have become a resident among you.” The Midrashic explanation is: “If you will agree then I am a stranger. If not, I will be as a resident and will rightfully take it. For God has told me, “To your descendants I will give this land.”", "גר ותושב אנכי עמכם. גר מארץ אחרת, ונתישבתי עמכם. ומדרש אגדה, אם תרצו הריני גר, ואם לאו אהיה תושב ואטלנה מן הדין, שאמר לי הקב\"ה לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת:"], ["The possession of a grave", "[Meaning:] the possession of land to serve as a burial place.", "אחוזת קבר. אחוזת קרקע לבית הקברות:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיַּעֲנוּ בְנֵי־חֵת אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר לוֹ", "en": "The sons of Cheis replied to Avraham saying to him,", "c": []}], [{"he": "שְׁמָעֵנוּ אֲדֹנִי נְשִׂיא אֱלֹקִים אַתָּה בְּתוֹכֵנוּ בְּמִבְחַר קְבָרֵינוּ קְבֹר אֶת־מֵתֶךָ אִישׁ מִמֶּנּוּ אֶת־קִבְרוֹ לֹא־יִכְלֶה מִמְּךָ מִקְּבֹר מֵתֶךָ", "en": "Hear us my master, you are a prince of God in our midst. Bury your dead in the choicest of our grave sites. No man among us will deny his grave site from you to bury your dead.", "c": [["Will not deny", "[Meaning:] will not withhold as in, “You will not withhold Your pity” and as in “The downpour was withheld.”", "לא יכלה. לא ימנע, כמו לֹא תִכְלָא רַחֲמֶיךָ (תהלים מ, יב), וכמו וַיִכָּלֵא הַגֶּשֶׁם (בראשית ח, ב):"]]}], [{"he": "וַיָּקָם אַבְרָהָם וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ לְעַם־הָאָרֶץ לִבְנֵי־חֵת", "en": "Avraham rose and bowed to the people of the land, the sons of Cheis.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיְדַבֵּר אִתָּם לֵאמֹר אִם־יֵשׁ אֶת־נַפְשְׁכֶם לִקְבֹּר אֶת־מֵתִי מִלְּפָנַי שְׁמָעוּנִי וּפִגְעוּ־לִי בְּעֶפְרוֹן בֶּן־צֹחַר", "en": "Avraham spoke to them, saying, If it is really your will that I bury my dead from my presence, listen to me and intercede for me with Ephron, son of Tzochar.", "c": [["Your will", "[Meaning:] your will.", "נפשכם. רצונכם:"], ["And intercede for me", "A term denoting a request as in “Do not entreat me.”", "ופגעו לי. לשון בקשה, כמו אַל תִּפְגְּעִי בִי (רות א, טז):"]]}], [{"he": "וְיִתֶּן־לִי אֶת־מְעָרַת הַמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ אֲשֶׁר בִּקְצֵה שָׂדֵהוּ בְּכֶסֶף מָלֵא יִתְּנֶנָּה לִי בְּתוֹכְכֶם לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר", "en": "Let him give me the Machpeilah [double] cave, which belongs to him, which is at the end of his field. Let him give [sell] it to me for its full value, as a grave site among you.", "c": [["Machpeilah", "I.e., a house with an upper level above it. Another explanation: It is doubled with couples.", "המכפלה. בית ועליה על גביו. דבר אחר, שכפולה בזוגות (עירובין נג.):"], ["For its full value", "[Meaning:] its full value. Similarly, Dovid said to Arnun, “For its full value.”", "בכסף מלא. אשלם כל שוויה, וכן דוד אמר לַאַרְוָנה בְּכֶסֶף מָלֵא (דברי הימים־א כא, כד):"]]}], [{"he": "וְעֶפְרוֹן יֹשֵׁב בְּתוֹךְ בְּנֵי־חֵת וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן הַחִתִּי אֶת־אַבְרָהָם בְּאָזְנֵי בְנֵי־חֵת לְכֹל בָּאֵי שַׁעַר־עִירוֹ לֵאמֹר", "en": "Ephron lived in the midst of the sons of Cheis, Ephron the Chitite replied to Avraham in the ears [audience] of the sons of Cheis, for all who came to the city gate, saying,", "c": [["Ephron lived", "It [ישֵׁב] is written [with a vav] missing. [This is because] on that day they appointed him [to be] an officer over them. Because of the exaltedness of Avraham who needed him [to purchase the land] he was raised to an important position.", "ועפרון ישב. כתיב חסר, אותו היום מנוהו שוטר עליהם, מפני חשיבותו של אברהם שהיה צריך לו, עלה לגדולה:"], ["For all who came to the city gate", "For they all left their work and came to pay their respects to Sarah.", "לכל באי שער עירו. שכולן בטלו ממלאכתן, ובאו לגמול חסד לשרה:"]]}], [{"he": "לֹא־אֲדֹנִי שְׁמָעֵנִי הַשָּׂדֶה נָתַתִּי לָךְ וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ לְךָ נְתַתִּיהָ לְעֵינֵי בְנֵי־עַמִּי נְתַתִּיהָ לָּךְ קְבֹר מֵתֶךָ", "en": "No, my master, hear me: I have given you the field, and the cave that is in it, I have [also] given to you. Before the eyes of the sons of my people I have given it to you. Bury your dead.", "c": [["No, my master", "“You will not buy it for money, [but. .]", "לא אדני. לא תקנה אותה בדמים:"], ["I have given you", "As though I have already given it to you.", "נתתי לך. הרי הוא כמו שנתתיה לך:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ אַבְרָהָם לִפְנֵי עַם הָאָרֶץ", "en": "Avraham bowed to the people of the land.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיְדַבֵּר אֶל־עֶפְרוֹן בְּאָזְנֵי עַם־הָאָרֶץ לֵאמֹר אַךְ אִם־אַתָּה לוּ שְׁמָעֵנִי נָתַתִּי כֶּסֶף הַשָּׂדֶה קַח מִמֶּנִּי וְאֶקְבְּרָה אֶת־מֵתִי שָׁמָּה", "en": "He spoke to Ephron in the ears [audience] of the people of the land saying, If you will only listen to me. I have given the money for the field. Take it from me and I will bury my dead there.", "c": [["If you will only listen to me", "“You tell me to listen to you and to take [the cave] without payment. I do not wish this.”", "אך אם אתה לו שמעני. אתה אומר לי לשמוע לך וליקח בחנם, אני אי אפשי בכך:"], ["If you will only listen to me", "[Meaning:] “Would that you listen to me.”", "אך אם אתה לוּ שמעני. הלואי ותשמעני:"], ["I have given", "Donne [“I am giving”] in Old French. “I have it available and I wish that I had already given it to you.”", "נתתי. דוני\"ש בלע\"ז, מוכן הוא אצלי, והלואי נתתי לך כבר:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר לוֹ", "en": "Ephron replied to Avraham, saying to him,", "c": []}], [{"he": "אֲדֹנִי שְׁמָעֵנִי אֶרֶץ אַרְבַּע מֵאֹת שֶׁקֶל־כֶּסֶף בֵּינִי וּבֵינְךָ מַה־הִוא וְאֶת־מֵתְךָ קְבֹר", "en": "My master, hear me. A land [worth] four hundred silver shekel—what is that between me and you? Bury your dead.", "c": [["Between me and you", "Between two friends such as we are, what significance does it have? None! Disregard the sale [for now] and bury your dead!", "ביני ובינך. בין שני אוהבים כמונו, מה היא חשובה לכלום, אלא הנח את המכר, ואת מתך קבור:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אַבְרָהָם אֶל־עֶפְרוֹן וַיִּשְׁקֹל אַבְרָהָם לְעֶפְרֹן אֶת־הַכֶּסֶף אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר בְּאָזְנֵי בְנֵי־חֵת אַרְבַּע מֵאוֹת שֶׁקֶל כֶּסֶף עֹבֵר לַסֹּחֵר", "en": "Avraham listened to Ephron, and Avraham weighed out for Ephron the silver that he spoke of in the hearing of the sons of Cheis, four hundred silver shekel, negotiable currency.", "c": [["Avraham weighed out for Ephron", "[עֶפְרֹן is spelled] without a vav because he said much and did not do even a little, for he took superior shekels from him—centenars, as it is said, “Negotiable currency,” i.e., they are accepted as a shekel everywhere for there are places whose shekels are superior which are centenars in Old French.", "וישקל אברהם לעפרן. חסר וי\"ו, לפי שאמר הרבה ואפילו מעט לא עשה, שנטל ממנו שקלים גדולים שהן קנטרין שנאמר עובר לסוחר, שמתקבלים בשקל בכל מקום, ויש מקום ששקליהן גדולים שהן קנטרין, (בבא מציעא פז. בכורות נ.), צנטיאר\"ש בלע\"ז:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיָּקָם שְׂדֵה עֶפְרוֹן אֲשֶׁר בַּמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר לִפְנֵי מַמְרֵא הַשָּׂדֶה וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ וְכָל־הָעֵץ אֲשֶׁר בַּשָּׂדֶה אֲשֶׁר בְּכָל־גְּבֻלוֹ סָבִיב", "en": "The field of Ephron was established [as Avraham’s possession], [the field] which was in Machpeilah, facing Mamrei; [this included] the field, the cave that was in it, and all the trees that were in the field that were in the entire circumference of its boundaries.", "c": [["The field of Ephron was established", "It was elevated [in importance] for it left the possession of a commoner to [become] the possession of a king. The simple meaning of the verse is: The field and the cave within it and all the trees came into Avraham’s possession, etc.", "ויקם שדה עפרון. תקומה היתה לו, שיצא מיד הדיוט ליד מלך. ופשוטו של מקרא, ויקם השדה והמערה אשר בו וכל העץ לאברהם למקנָה וגו':"]]}], [{"he": "לְאַבְרָהָם לְמִקְנָה לְעֵינֵי בְנֵי־חֵת בְּכֹל בָּאֵי שַׁעַר־עִירוֹ", "en": "This became Avraham’s [possession] through a purchase before the eyes of the sons of Cheis, all who had come to the gate of his city.", "c": [["All who had come to the gate of his city", "[I.e.,] amongst all of them and in the presence of all, he gave him possession.", "בכל באי שער עירו. בקרב כולם ובמעמד כולם הקנהו לו:"]]}], [{"he": "וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן קָבַר אַבְרָהָם אֶת־שָׂרָה אִשְׁתּוֹ אֶל־מְעָרַת שְׂדֵה הַמַּכְפֵּלָה עַל־פְּנֵי מַמְרֵא הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן", "en": "After that Avraham buried his wife Sarah in the cave of the Machpeilah field, which faces Mamrei, which is Chevron, in the land of Canaan.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיָּקָם הַשָּׂדֶה וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ לְאַבְרָהָם לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר מֵאֵת בְּנֵי־חֵת", "en": "The field and its cave was established as Avraham’s possession as a gravesite, by the sons of Cheis.", "c": []}]];
const C3S23_LESSONS=[{"id": "cs23-1", "title": "The life of Sarah", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 23:1–6", "parts": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "phrases": [["וַיִּהְיוּ חַיֵּי שָׂרָה מֵאָה שָׁנָה וְעֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה וְשֶׁבַע שָׁנִים שְׁנֵי חַיֵּי שָׂרָה", "The lifetime of Sarah consisted of one hundred years, twenty years and seven years. [These were] the years of Sarah’s life."], ["וַתָּמָת שָׂרָה בְּקִרְיַת אַרְבַּע הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן וַיָּבֹא אַבְרָהָם לִסְפֹּד לְשָׂרָה וְלִבְכֹּתָהּ", "Sarah died in Kiryas Arba, which is Chevron, in the land of Canaan. Avraham came to eulogize Sarah and to weep for her."], ["וַיָּקָם אַבְרָהָם מֵעַל פְּנֵי מֵתוֹ וַיְדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי־חֵת לֵאמֹר", "Avraham rose from the presence of his dead, and spoke to the sons of Cheis saying,"], ["גֵּר־וְתוֹשָׁב אָנֹכִי עִמָּכֶם תְּנוּ לִי אֲחֻזַּת־קֶבֶר עִמָּכֶם וְאֶקְבְּרָה מֵתִי מִלְּפָנָי", "I am a foreigner and a resident among you. Grant me the possession of a grave site with you, so that I may bury my dead from my presence."], ["וַיַּעֲנוּ בְנֵי־חֵת אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר לוֹ", "The sons of Cheis replied to Avraham saying to him,"], ["שְׁמָעֵנוּ אֲדֹנִי נְשִׂיא אֱלֹקִים אַתָּה בְּתוֹכֵנוּ בְּמִבְחַר קְבָרֵינוּ קְבֹר אֶת־מֵתֶךָ אִישׁ מִמֶּנּוּ אֶת־קִבְרוֹ לֹא־יִכְלֶה מִמְּךָ מִקְּבֹר מֵתֶךָ", "Hear us my master, you are a prince of God in our midst. Bury your dead in the choicest of our grave sites. No man among us will deny his grave site from you to bury your dead."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 2, "note": ["Rashi", "“In Kiryas Arba” — So called because of the four giants that were there, Achiman, Sheishai, Talmai, and their father."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "The lifetime of Sarah consisted of one hundred years, twenty years and seven years. [These…", "tiles": ["וַיִּהְיוּ", "חַיֵּי", "שָׂרָה", "מֵאָה"], "decoys": ["קְבֹר"], "id": "cs23-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How old was Sarah when she passed away?", "opts": ["127", "100", "90", "175"], "a": 0, "ex": "Rashi: at 100 she was like 20 in sin, and at 20 like 7 in beauty. All her years were equally good.", "id": "cs23-1-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where did Sarah pass away?", "opts": ["Kiryas Arba, which is Chevron", "Be'er Sheva", "Charan", "Shechem"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-1-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 2, "to": 6, "note": ["Rashi", "“I am a foreigner and a resident among you” — “A stranger from another land and I have become a resident among you.” The Midrashic explanation is: “If you will agree then I am a stranger. If not, I will be as a resident and will rightfully take it."], "mref": 2}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did the sons of Cheis call Avraham?", "opts": ["A prince of Hashem among us", "A stranger", "A king", "A shepherd"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-1-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (23:4)", "before": "גֵּר־וְתוֹשָׁב אָנֹכִי עִמָּכֶם תְּנוּ לִי אֲחֻזַּת־קֶבֶר עִמָּכֶם וְאֶקְבְּרָה מֵתִי", "after": "", "opts": ["מִלְּפָנָי", "יִשְׁלַח", "בִּקְצֵה"], "a": 0, "ex": "גֵּר־וְתוֹשָׁב אָנֹכִי עִמָּכֶם תְּנוּ לִי אֲחֻזַּת־קֶבֶר עִמָּכֶם וְאֶקְבְּרָה מֵתִי מִלְּפָנָי", "id": "cs23-1-5"}]}, {"id": "cs23-2", "title": "Avraham asks for the cave", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 23:7–11", "parts": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10], "phrases": [["וַיָּקָם אַבְרָהָם וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ לְעַם־הָאָרֶץ לִבְנֵי־חֵת", "Avraham rose and bowed to the people of the land, the sons of Cheis."], ["וַיְדַבֵּר אִתָּם לֵאמֹר אִם־יֵשׁ אֶת־נַפְשְׁכֶם לִקְבֹּר אֶת־מֵתִי מִלְּפָנַי שְׁמָעוּנִי וּפִגְעוּ־לִי בְּעֶפְרוֹן בֶּן־צֹחַר", "Avraham spoke to them, saying, If it is really your will that I bury my dead from my presence, listen to me and intercede for me with Ephron, son of Tzochar."], ["וְיִתֶּן־לִי אֶת־מְעָרַת הַמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ אֲשֶׁר בִּקְצֵה שָׂדֵהוּ בְּכֶסֶף מָלֵא יִתְּנֶנָּה לִי בְּתוֹכְכֶם לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר", "Let him give me the Machpeilah [double] cave, which belongs to him, which is at the end of his field. Let him give [sell] it to me for its full value, as a grave site among you."], ["וְעֶפְרוֹן יֹשֵׁב בְּתוֹךְ בְּנֵי־חֵת וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן הַחִתִּי אֶת־אַבְרָהָם בְּאָזְנֵי בְנֵי־חֵת לְכֹל בָּאֵי שַׁעַר־עִירוֹ לֵאמֹר", "Ephron lived in the midst of the sons of Cheis, Ephron the Chitite replied to Avraham in the ears [audience] of the sons of Cheis, for all who came to the city gate, saying,"], ["לֹא־אֲדֹנִי שְׁמָעֵנִי הַשָּׂדֶה נָתַתִּי לָךְ וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ לְךָ נְתַתִּיהָ לְעֵינֵי בְנֵי־עַמִּי נְתַתִּיהָ לָּךְ קְבֹר מֵתֶךָ", "No, my master, hear me: I have given you the field, and the cave that is in it, I have [also] given to you. Before the eyes of the sons of my people I have given it to you. Bury your dead."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 3, "note": ["Rashi", "“Machpeilah” — I.e., a house with an upper level above it. Another explanation: It is doubled with couples."], "mref": 6}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "Avraham rose and bowed to the people of the land, the sons of Cheis.", "tiles": ["וַיָּקָם", "אַבְרָהָם", "וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ", "לְעַם־הָאָרֶץ"], "decoys": ["נְתַתִּיהָ"], "id": "cs23-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Which cave did Avraham ask for?", "opts": ["Me'aras HaMachpelah", "The cave of Eliyahu", "A cave in Be'er Sheva", "A cave near Charan"], "a": 0, "ex": "Machpelah means 'double': a cave with an upper level and a lower one, or a cave for couples (Rashi).", "id": "cs23-2-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Who owned the cave?", "opts": ["Ephron, son of Tzochar", "Avimelech", "Malki-Tzedek", "Lot"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-2-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 3, "to": 5, "note": null, "mref": 9}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Avraham asked to pay the full price for the cave.", "a": true, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-2-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (23:9)", "before": "וְיִתֶּן־לִי אֶת־מְעָרַת הַמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ אֲשֶׁר בִּקְצֵה שָׂדֵהוּ בְּכֶסֶף מָלֵא יִתְּנֶנָּה לִי בְּתוֹכְכֶם", "after": "", "opts": ["לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר", "בֶּקַע", "מִשָּׁם"], "a": 0, "ex": "וְיִתֶּן־לִי אֶת־מְעָרַת הַמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ אֲשֶׁר בִּקְצֵה שָׂדֵהוּ בְּכֶסֶף מָלֵא יִתְּנֶנָּה לִי בְּתוֹכְכֶם לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר", "id": "cs23-2-5"}]}, {"id": "cs23-3", "title": "Four hundred shekel", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 23:12–16", "parts": [11, 12, 13, 14, 15], "phrases": [["וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ אַבְרָהָם לִפְנֵי עַם הָאָרֶץ", "Avraham bowed to the people of the land."], ["וַיְדַבֵּר אֶל־עֶפְרוֹן בְּאָזְנֵי עַם־הָאָרֶץ לֵאמֹר אַךְ אִם־אַתָּה לוּ שְׁמָעֵנִי נָתַתִּי כֶּסֶף הַשָּׂדֶה קַח מִמֶּנִּי וְאֶקְבְּרָה אֶת־מֵתִי שָׁמָּה", "He spoke to Ephron in the ears [audience] of the people of the land saying, If you will only listen to me. I have given the money for the field. Take it from me and I will bury my dead there."], ["וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר לוֹ", "Ephron replied to Avraham, saying to him,"], ["אֲדֹנִי שְׁמָעֵנִי אֶרֶץ אַרְבַּע מֵאֹת שֶׁקֶל־כֶּסֶף בֵּינִי וּבֵינְךָ מַה־הִוא וְאֶת־מֵתְךָ קְבֹר", "My master, hear me. A land [worth] four hundred silver shekel—what is that between me and you? Bury your dead."], ["וַיִּשְׁמַע אַבְרָהָם אֶל־עֶפְרוֹן וַיִּשְׁקֹל אַבְרָהָם לְעֶפְרֹן אֶת־הַכֶּסֶף אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר בְּאָזְנֵי בְנֵי־חֵת אַרְבַּע מֵאוֹת שֶׁקֶל כֶּסֶף עֹבֵר לַסֹּחֵר", "Avraham listened to Ephron, and Avraham weighed out for Ephron the silver that he spoke of in the hearing of the sons of Cheis, four hundred silver shekel, negotiable currency."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Rashi", "“If you will only listen to me” — “You tell me to listen to you and to take [the cave] without payment. I do not wish this.”"], "mref": 11}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "Avraham bowed to the people of the land.", "tiles": ["וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ", "אַבְרָהָם", "לִפְנֵי", "עַם"], "decoys": ["אִם־אַתָּה"], "id": "cs23-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How much silver did Avraham pay Ephron?", "opts": ["400 shekel", "40 shekel", "100 shekel", "Nothing; it was a gift"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-3-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Ephron said a lot but in the end took full payment.", "a": true, "ex": "Rashi: he said much but did not even do a little; he took large shekels.", "id": "cs23-3-3"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What does 'עובר לסוחר' mean?", "opts": ["Coins accepted by merchants everywhere", "A gift", "A loan", "Gold jewelry"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-3-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (23:14)", "before": "וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר", "after": "", "opts": ["לוֹ", "וּמֵאֶרֶץ", "וַתִּשְׁאַב"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַיַּעַן עֶפְרוֹן אֶת־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר לוֹ", "id": "cs23-3-5"}]}, {"id": "cs23-4", "title": "Avraham's field and cave", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 23:17–20", "parts": [16, 17, 18, 19], "phrases": [["וַיָּקָם שְׂדֵה עֶפְרוֹן אֲשֶׁר בַּמַּכְפֵּלָה אֲשֶׁר לִפְנֵי מַמְרֵא הַשָּׂדֶה וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ וְכָל־הָעֵץ אֲשֶׁר בַּשָּׂדֶה אֲשֶׁר בְּכָל־גְּבֻלוֹ סָבִיב", "The field of Ephron was established [as Avraham’s possession], [the field] which was in Machpeilah, facing Mamrei; [this included] the field, the cave that was in it, and all the trees that were in the field that were in the entire circumference of its boundaries."], ["לְאַבְרָהָם לְמִקְנָה לְעֵינֵי בְנֵי־חֵת בְּכֹל בָּאֵי שַׁעַר־עִירוֹ", "This became Avraham’s [possession] through a purchase before the eyes of the sons of Cheis, all who had come to the gate of his city."], ["וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן קָבַר אַבְרָהָם אֶת־שָׂרָה אִשְׁתּוֹ אֶל־מְעָרַת שְׂדֵה הַמַּכְפֵּלָה עַל־פְּנֵי מַמְרֵא הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן", "After that Avraham buried his wife Sarah in the cave of the Machpeilah field, which faces Mamrei, which is Chevron, in the land of Canaan."], ["וַיָּקָם הַשָּׂדֶה וְהַמְּעָרָה אֲשֶׁר־בּוֹ לְאַבְרָהָם לַאֲחֻזַּת־קָבֶר מֵאֵת בְּנֵי־חֵת", "The field and its cave was established as Avraham’s possession as a gravesite, by the sons of Cheis."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Rashi", "“The field of Ephron was established” — It was elevated [in importance] for it left the possession of a commoner to [become] the possession of a king. The simple meaning of the verse is: The field and the cave within it and all the trees came into Avraham’s possession, etc."], "mref": 16}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "The field of Ephron was established [as Avraham’s possession], [the field] which was in Ma…", "tiles": ["וַיָּקָם", "שְׂדֵה", "עֶפְרוֹן", "אֲשֶׁר"], "decoys": ["לְעֵינֵי"], "id": "cs23-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What was included in the sale?", "opts": ["The field, the cave and all its trees", "Only the cave", "Only the field", "A house in Chevron"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-4-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Me'aras HaMachpelah is in Chevron.", "a": true, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-4-3"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Who did Avraham bury in Me'aras HaMachpelah here?", "opts": ["Sarah his wife", "Terach", "Lot", "Nachor"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs23-4-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (23:19)", "before": "וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן קָבַר אַבְרָהָם אֶת־שָׂרָה אִשְׁתּוֹ אֶל־מְעָרַת שְׂדֵה הַמַּכְפֵּלָה עַל־פְּנֵי מַמְרֵא הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ", "after": "", "opts": ["כְּנָעַן", "לִגְמַלֶּיךָ", "הָאִישׁ"], "a": 0, "ex": "וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן קָבַר אַבְרָהָם אֶת־שָׂרָה אִשְׁתּוֹ אֶל־מְעָרַת שְׂדֵה הַמַּכְפֵּלָה עַל־פְּנֵי מַמְרֵא הִוא חֶבְרוֹן בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן", "id": "cs23-4-5"}]}];
const C3S24_SECTIONS=[[{"he": "וְאַבְרָהָם זָקֵן בָּא בַּיָּמִים וַה' בֵּרַךְ אֶת־אַבְרָהָם בַּכֹּל", "en": "Avraham was old, advanced in days [years], and Adonoy had blessed Avraham in all things.", "c": [["Blessed Avraham in all things", "בַּכֹּל is numerically equal to בֵּן [son], and since he had a son he needed to find a wife for him.", "ברך את אברהם בכל. בַכֹּל עולה בגימטריא בן, ומאחר שהיה לו בן, היה צריך להשיאו אשה:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמֶר אַבְרָהָם אֶל־עַבְדּוֹ זְקַן בֵּיתוֹ הַמֹּשֵׁל בְּכָל־אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ שִׂים־נָא יָדְךָ תַּחַת יְרֵכִי", "en": "Avraham said to his servant, the senior [servant] of his household, who was in charge of all that he owned, Place your hand under my thigh.", "c": [["The senior [servant] of his household", "Since [the word זְקַן] is in the construct state it is punctuated זְקַן [rather than זָקֵן].", "זקן ביתו. לפי שהוא דבוק נקוד זְקַן:"], ["Under my thigh", "Since one who takes an oath requires holding a sacred object in his hand such as a Sefer Torah or Tefillin, and circumcision was his first mitzvah and came to him through pain, it was, therefore, dear to him, and he took it.", "תחת ירכי. לפי שהנשבע צריך שיטול בידו חפץ של מצוה, כגון ספר תורה, או תפילין (שבועות לח:), והמילה היתה מצוה ראשונה לו, ובאה לו על ידי צער, והיתה חביבה עליו, ונטלה:"]]}], [{"he": "וְאַשְׁבִּיעֲךָ בַּה' אֱלֹקֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם וֵאלֹקֵי הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר לֹא־תִקַּח אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי מִבְּנוֹת הַכְּנַעֲנִי אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי יוֹשֵׁב בְּקִרְבּוֹ", "en": "I will have you swear by Adonoy, God of heaven and God of earth, that you will not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom I live.", "c": []}], [{"he": "כִּי אֶל־אַרְצִי וְאֶל־מוֹלַדְתִּי תֵּלֵךְ וְלָקַחְתָּ אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי לְיִצְחָק", "en": "Instead, to my [native] land, to my birthplace, shall you go, and take a wife for my son, for Yitzchok,", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו הָעֶבֶד אוּלַי לֹא־תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרַי אֶל־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הֶהָשֵׁב אָשִׁיב אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־יָצָאתָ מִשָּׁם", "en": "The servant said to him, Perhaps the woman will not want to come back with me to this land? Shall I bring your son back to the land from where you came?", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו אַבְרָהָם הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ פֶּן־תָּשִׁיב אֶת־בְּנִי שָׁמָּה", "en": "Avraham said to him, Take care, not to bring my son back there.", "c": []}], [{"he": "ה' אֱלֹקֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם אֲשֶׁר לְקָחַנִי מִבֵּית אָבִי וּמֵאֶרֶץ מוֹלַדְתִּי וַאֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר־לִי וַאֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע־לִי לֵאמֹר לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הוּא יִשְׁלַח מַלְאָכוֹ לְפָנֶיךָ וְלָקַחְתָּ אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי מִשָּׁם", "en": "Adonoy, God of heaven, Who took me from my father’s house, and from the land of my birth, Who spoke to me, and Who swore to me, saying, To your descendants I will give this land—He will send His angel before you, and you shall take a wife for my son from there.", "c": [["Adonoy, God of heaven Who took me from my father’s house", "Here he did not say “and the God of earth,” whereas, above he did say, “And I will have you swear, etc.” He, [Avraham] [in effect,] said to him [the servant], “Now He is the God of heaven and earth for I have made Him current on everyone’s tongue.” But at the time that He took me from my father’s house, He was the God of the heavens but not the God of the earth because humanity did not acknowledge Him and His Name was not common on earth.", "ה' אלקי השמים אשר לקחני מבית אבי. ולא אמר ואלקי הארץ, ולמעלה אמר ואשביעך וגו', אמר לו עכשיו הוא אלקי השמים ואלקי הארץ, שהרגלתיו בפי הבריות, אבל כשלקחני מבית אבי, היה אלקי השמים ולא אלקי הארץ, שלא היו באי עולם מכירים בו, ושמו לא היה רגיל בארץ:"], ["From my father’s house", "[I.e.,] from Charan.", "מבית אבי. מחרן:"], ["And from the land of my birth", "[I.e.,] from Ur Kasdim.", "ומארץ מולדתי. מאור כשדים:"], ["Who spoke to me", "[Here לִי means] concerning me. As in “Which he spoke concerning me.” So, too, every time לִי, לוֹ, לָהֶם which follow the verb דִבּוּר —speak are to be explained as עַל — concerning, and their Targum is עֲלַי, עֲלוֹהִי, עֲלֵיהוֹן because the verb דִבּוּר does not take לִי, לוֹ, לָהֶם but, rather אֵלַי, אֵלָיו, אֲלֵיהֶם and their Targum is עִמִּי, עִמֵּיהּ, עִמְּהוֹן. However, following the verb אמר [say] the terms לִי, לוֹ, לָהֶם are used.", "ואשר דבר לי. לצורכי, כמו אשר דבר עלי. וכן כל לי ולו ולהם הסמוכים אצל דבור, מפורשים בלשון על, ותרגום שלהם (רצונו שדרך התרגום להשתמש למ\"ד במקום בעבור וק\"ל), עלי, עלוהי, עליהון, שאין נופל אצל דיבור לשון לי, ולו, ולהם, אלא אלי, אליו, אליהם. ותרגום שלהם עִמי, עמיה, עמהון, אבל אצל אמירה נופל לשון לי, ולו, ולהם:"], ["And who swore to me", "At the covenant “Between the Pieces.”", "ואשר נשבע לי. בין הבתרים:"]]}], [{"he": "וְאִם־לֹא תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרֶיךָ וְנִקִּיתָ מִשְּׁבֻעָתִי זֹאת רַק אֶת־בְּנִי לֹא תָשֵׁב שָׁמָּה", "en": "If the woman does not want to come back with you, you are absolved from this oath to me. But do not bring my son back there.", "c": [["You are absolved from this oath, etc", "And you may take a wife for him from the daughters of Aner, Eshkol and Mamrei.", "ונקית משבועתי וגו'. וקח לו אשה מבנות ענר אשכול וממרא:"], ["But my son, etc", "The word רַק is used to denote an exception. [I.e.,] “My son will not return there, but, Yaakov my grandson will eventually return.”", "רק את בני וגו'. רק מיעוט הוא, בני אינו חוזר, אבל יעקב בן בני סופו לחזור:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיָּשֶׂם הָעֶבֶד אֶת־יָדוֹ תַּחַת יֶרֶךְ אַבְרָהָם אֲדֹנָיו וַיִּשָּׁבַע לוֹ עַל־הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה", "en": "The servant placed his hand under the thigh of Avraham, his master, and swore to him regarding this matter.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיִּקַּח הָעֶבֶד עֲשָׂרָה גְמַלִּים מִגְּמַלֵּי אֲדֹנָיו וַיֵּלֶךְ וְכָל־טוּב אֲדֹנָיו בְּיָדוֹ וַיָּקָם וַיֵּלֶךְ אֶל־אֲרַם נַהֲרַיִם אֶל־עִיר נָחוֹר", "en": "The servant took ten camels from his master’s camels and departed, and all the property of his master was in his hand. He rose and went to Aram Naharayim; to the city of Nachor.", "c": [["From his master’s camels", "They were distinguishable from other camels, for they would go out only muzzled, out of concern for robbery that they not graze in others’ fields.", "מגמלי אדוניו. נִיכָּרִין היו משאר גמלים, שהיו יוצאין זמומין (ב\"ר נט, י), מפני הגזל, שלא ירעו בשדות אחרים:"], ["And all the property of his master was in his hand", "He [Avraham] wrote a gift-deed to Yitzchok of all his possessions so that they would be eager to send their daughter to him.", "וכל טוב אדוניו בידו. שטר מתנה כתב ליצחק על כל אשר לו, כדי שיקפצו לשלוח לו בתם (שם יא):"], ["Aram Naharayim", "It is situated between two rivers.", "ארם נהרים. בין שתי נהרות יושבת:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיַּבְרֵךְ הַגְּמַלִּים מִחוּץ לָעִיר אֶל־בְּאֵר הַמָּיִם לְעֵת עֶרֶב לְעֵת צֵאת הַשֹּׁאֲבֹת", "en": "He made the camels kneel outside the city, beside a well of water, in the evening, at the time the women go out to draw water.", "c": [["He made the camels kneel", "[Meaning:] he made them lie down.", "ויברך הגמלים. הרביצם:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמַר ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם הַקְרֵה־נָא לְפָנַי הַיּוֹם וַעֲשֵׂה־חֶסֶד עִם אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם", "en": "He said, Adonoy, God of my master, Avraham, be present before me today, and act kindly with my master, Avraham.", "c": []}], [{"he": "הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי נִצָּב עַל־עֵין הַמָּיִם וּבְנוֹת אַנְשֵׁי הָעִיר יֹצְאֹת לִשְׁאֹב מָיִם", "en": "Behold, here I stand by this well of water, and the daughters of the townsmen are coming out to draw water.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וְהָיָה הַנַּעֲרָ אֲשֶׁר אֹמַר אֵלֶיהָ הַטִּי־נָא כַדֵּךְ וְאֶשְׁתֶּה וְאָמְרָה שְׁתֵה וְגַם־גְּמַלֶּיךָ אַשְׁקֶה אֹתָהּ הֹכַחְתָּ לְעַבְדְּךָ לְיִצְחָק וּבָהּ אֵדַע כִּי־עָשִׂיתָ חֶסֶד עִם־אֲדֹנִי", "en": "Let it be that the girl to whom I say, Please, tip over your pitcher that I may drink and she will say Drink, and I will also give your camels to drink, will be the one whom You have determined for your servant, Yitzchok. With her I will know that You have dealt kindly with my master.", "c": [["[She] will be the one whom You have determined", "She is fitting for him for she will perform kind deeds and is worthy to enter the house of Avraham. The term הֹכַחְתָּ means “You selected,” Approuvest in Old French.", "אותה הוכחת. ראויה היא לו, שתהא גומלת חסדים, וכדאי ליכנס בביתו של אברהם, ולשון הוכחת, ביררת, אפרוביש\"ט בלע\"ז:"], ["With her I will know", "This was a plea. [I.e.,] “Let me know through her…", "ובה אדע. לשון תחנה, הודע לי בה:"], ["That You have dealt kindly", "If she will be from his family and fit [to be a wife] for him, I will know that You have done kindness.", "כי עשית חסד. אם תהיה ממשפחתו והוגנת לו, אדע כי עשית חסד:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיְהִי־הוּא טֶרֶם כִּלָּה לְדַבֵּר וְהִנֵּה רִבְקָה יֹצֵאת אֲשֶׁר יֻלְּדָה לִבְתוּאֵל בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֵשֶׁת נָחוֹר אֲחִי אַבְרָהָם וְכַדָּהּ עַל־שִׁכְמָהּ", "en": "He had not yet finished speaking, and behold Rivkah came out. She had been born to Besu’eil, the son of Milkah, the wife of Nachor, Avraham’s brother. Her pitcher was on her shoulder.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וְהַנַּעֲרָ טֹבַת מַרְאֶה מְאֹד בְּתוּלָה וְאִישׁ לֹא יְדָעָהּ וַתֵּרֶד הָעַיְנָה וַתְּמַלֵּא כַדָּהּ וַתָּעַל", "en": "The girl was very fine, and unmarried. She went down to the well, filled her pitcher, and came up.", "c": [["A virgin", "[She was a virgin] at her maidenhood.", "בתולה. ממקום בתולים (ב\"ר ס, ה):"], ["No man had known her", "[She had no] unnatural relations. Since the gentile maidens guard their maidenhood and are promiscuous in unnatural ways, Scripture therefore testifies about her that she was innocent of all this.", "ואיש לא ידעה. שלא כדרכה, לפי שבנות הכנענים היו משמרות מקום בתוליהן, ומפקירות עצמן ממקום אחר, העיד על זו שנקייה מכל:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיָּרָץ הָעֶבֶד לִקְרָאתָהּ וַיֹּאמֶר הַגְמִיאִינִי נָא מְעַט־מַיִם מִכַּדֵּךְ", "en": "The servant ran toward her and said, Please let me sip a little water from your pitcher.", "c": [["The servant ran toward her", "Because he saw the water rise toward her.", "וירץ העבד לקראתה. לפי שראה שעלו המים לקראתה (ב\"ר שם):"], ["Please let me sip", "[הַגְמִיאִינִי is] from the term גְמִיעָה [sipping], humer in old French.", "הגמיאיני נא. לשון גמיעה, הומיי\"ר בלע\"ז:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתֹּאמֶר שְׁתֵה אֲדֹנִי וַתְּמַהֵר וַתֹּרֶד כַּדָּהּ עַל־יָדָהּ וַתַּשְׁקֵהוּ", "en": "She said, Drink, my master, and she quickly lowered her pitcher to her hand, and let him drink.", "c": [["[She] lowered her pitcher", "From her shoulder.", "ותרד כדה. מעל שכמה:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתְּכַל לְהַשְׁקֹתוֹ וַתֹּאמֶר גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ אֶשְׁאָב עַד אִם־כִּלּוּ לִשְׁתֹּת", "en": "When she had finished giving him to drink, she said, I will also draw water for your camels, until they will have finished drinking.", "c": [["Until they will have finished", "Here אִם is used to mean “that.” Onkelos translates it “they had enough” because that is the end of their drinking— when they have had enough to drink.", "עד אם כלו. הרי אם משמש בלשון אשר: אם כלו. תרגם אונקלוס די ספקון, שזו היא גמר שתייתן כששתו די ספוקן:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתְּמַהֵר וַתְּעַר כַּדָּהּ אֶל־הַשֹּׁקֶת וַתָּרָץ עוֹד אֶל־הַבְּאֵר לִשְׁאֹב וַתִּשְׁאַב לְכָל־גְּמַלָּיו", "en": "She quickly emptied her pitcher into the trough and she ran to the well again to draw water. and she drew water for all his camels.", "c": [["[She] emptied", "Meaning to pour out. This term is prevalent in the Mishnah: “One who pours from one vessel to another.” It is similarly found in Scripture, “Do not pour out my soul” [and,] “That he poured out his soul to death.”", "ותער. לשון נפיצה, והרבה יש בלשון משנה, המערה מכלי אל כלי, ובמקרא יש לו דומה אַל תְּעַר נַפְשִׁי (תהלים קמא, ח), אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱרָה לַמָּוֶת נַפְשׁוֹ (ישעיה נג, יב):"], ["The trough", "A hollowed out stone from which camels drink.", "השקת. אבן חלולה ששותים בה הגמלים:"]]}], [{"he": "וְהָאִישׁ מִשְׁתָּאֵה לָהּ מַחֲרִישׁ לָדַעַת הַהִצְלִיחַ ה' דַּרְכּוֹ אִם־לֹא", "en": "The man, wondering at her, remained silent, waiting to determine whether Adonoy had made his mission successful, or not.", "c": [["Wondering", "From the term שְׁאִיּה [desolated] as in “the cities become desolate, and the land becomes totally wasted.”", "משתאה. לשון שאיה, כמו שָׁאוּ עָרִים, תִּשָּׁאֶה שְׁמָמָה (ישעיה ו, יא.):"], ["Wondering", "[Meaning:] astounded and shocked because he saw his undertaking nearing success, yet he did not yet know whether or not she was of Avraham’s family. Do not wonder concerning the letter ת' in the word מִשְׁתָּאֵה, for there is not a single word whose first root-letter is a ש' which is used in the reflexive form where the letter ת' does not separate between two of the root-letters, as in the word מִשְׁתָּאֵה, or מִשְׁתּוֹלֵל, from the same root as שׁוֹלָל, or וַיִּשְׁתּוֹמֵם from the same root as שְׁמָמָה or וְיִּשְׁתַּמֵּר חֻקּוֹת עָמְרִי from the same root as וַיִּשְׁמֹר. Here, too, מִשְׁתָּאֵה is from the same root as תִּשָּׁאֶה. Now, you will find the term מְשׁוֹמֵם concerning a person who is shocked and dumbstruck and is deep in thought as in, “Concerning his day, נָשַׁמּוּ —there will be astonishment to those who come later,” or שׁוֹמּוּ שָׁמַיִם —“Let the heavens be astonished” or אֶשְׁתּוֹמֵם —“He was momentarily astonished.” Likewise should you explain the term שְׁאִיָּה concerning a shocked person and one who is deep in thought. [However,] Onkelos translates it from the term שְׁהִיָּה —waiting. “The man waited,” [i.e.] he stood in one spot and waited to see whether God had brought him success. [מִשְׁתָּאֵה] should not be translated שָׁתֵי — drinking for it [מִשְׁתָּאֵה] does not mean drinking, because the verb “drink” does not take an א'.", "משתאה. משתומם ומתבהל, על שראה דברו קרוב להצליח, אבל אינו יודע אם ממשפחת אברהם היא אם לאו. ואל תתמה בתי\"ו של משתאה, שאין לך תיבה שתחלת יסודה שי\"ן ומדברת בלשון מתפעל, שאין תי\"ו מפרידה בין שתי אותיות של עיקר היסוד, כגון משתאה מגזרת שאה, מִשְׁתּוֹלֵל (שם נט, טו) מגזרת שולל, וַיִּשְׁתּוֹמֵם (שם טז) מגזרת שממה, וְיִשְׁתַּמֵּר חֻקוֹת עָמְרִי (מיכה ו, טז) מגזרת וישמר, אף כאן משתאה מגזרת תשאה, וכשם שאתה מוצא לשון משומם באדם נבהל ונאלם ובעל מחשבות, כמו עַל יוֹמוֹ נָשַׁמּוּ אַחֲרוֹנִים (איוב יח, כ), שֹׁמּוּ שָׁמַיִם (ירמיה ב, יב), אֶשְׁתּוֹמֵם כְּשָׁעָה חֲדָה (דניאל ד, טז), כך תפרש לשון שאייה באדם בהול ובעל מחשבות. ואונקלוס תרגם לשון שהייה, וגברא שָׁהֵי, שוהא ועומד במקום אחד, לראות ההצליח ה' דרכו, ואין לתרגם שתי שהרי אינו לשון שתיה, שאין אל\"ף נופלת בלשון שתיה:"], ["Wondering at her", "[Meaning:] he was wondering about her, as in, “Say about me, ‘He is my brother’” and as in, “The people of the place asked about his wife.”", "משתאה לה. משתומם עליה, כמו אִמְרִי לִי אָחִי הוּא (בראשית כ, יג), וכמו וַיִּשְׁאֲלוּ אַנְשֵׁי הַמָּקוֹם לְאִשְׁתּוֹ (שם כו, ז):"]]}], [{"he": "וַיְהִי כַּאֲשֶׁר כִּלּוּ הַגְּמַלִּים לִשְׁתּוֹת וַיִּקַּח הָאִישׁ נֶזֶם זָהָב בֶּקַע מִשְׁקָלוֹ וּשְׁנֵי צְמִידִים עַל־יָדֶיהָ עֲשָׂרָה זָהָב מִשְׁקָלָם", "en": "When the camels had finished drinking, the man took a gold nose ring, weighing half a shekel, and two bracelets for her arms, weighing ten gold shekel.", "c": [["Half a shekel", "This is symbolic of the shekels of Israel [which were] a בֶקַע [half-shekel] per head.", "בקע. רמז לשקלי ישראל, בֶּקַע לַגֻּלְגֹלֶת:"], ["And two bracelets", "Symbolic of the two linked [מצוּמָדוֹת] Tablets.", "ושני צמידים. רמז לשני לוחות מצומדות:"], ["Weighing ten gold shekels", "Symbolic of the Ten Commandments [inscribed] in them.", "עשרה זהב משקלם. רמז לעשרת הדברות שבהן:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמֶר בַּת־מִי אַתְּ הַגִּידִי נָא לִי הֲיֵשׁ בֵּית־אָבִיךְ מָקוֹם לָנוּ לָלִין", "en": "He said to her, Whose daughter are you? Please tell me. Is there place in your father’s house for us to spend the night.", "c": [["He said to her, “Whose daughter are you?”", "He asked her this after giving her [the gifts] because he had confidence that due to Avraham’s merit God had brought him success.", "ויאמר בת מי את. לאחר שנתן לה שָׁאַלָה, לפי שהיה בטוח בזכותו של אברהם שהצליח הקב\"ה דרכו:"], ["To spend the night", "[לִין] refers to one night’s lodging. לִין is a noun. However, she used the verb לָלוּן referring to many lodgings.", "ללין. לינה אחת, לין שֵׁם דבר, והיא אמרה ללון כמה לינות:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו בַּת־בְּתוּאֵל אָנֹכִי בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה לְנָחוֹר", "en": "She said to him, I am the daughter of Besueil, the son of Milkah, whom she bore to Nachor.", "c": [["The daughter of Besueil", "She responded to his first [question] first and the last [question] last.", "בת בתואל. השיבתו על ראשון ראשון ועל אחרון אחרון:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו גַּם־תֶּבֶן גַּם־מִסְפּוֹא רַב עִמָּנוּ גַּם־מָקוֹם לָלוּן", "en": "She said to him, We have plenty of straw and fodder, and also a place to spend the night.", "c": [["Fodder", "All camels’ foods are called מִסְפּוֹא, such as hay and barley.", "מספוא. כל מאכל הגמלים קרוי מספוא, כגון תבן ושעורים:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיִּקֹּד הָאִישׁ וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ לַה'", "en": "The man bowed [his head] and prostrated himself to Adonoy.", "c": []}], [{"he": "וַיֹּאמֶר בָּרוּךְ ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר לֹא־עָזַב חַסְדּוֹ וַאֲמִתּוֹ מֵעִם אֲדֹנִי אָנֹכִי בַּדֶּרֶךְ נָחַנִי ה' בֵּית אֲחֵי אֲדֹנִי", "en": "He said, Blessed is Adonoy, God of my master, Avraham, Who has not abandoned His kindness and truth [in dealing] with my master. I am still on the road and Adonoy has led me to the house of my master’s brethren.", "c": [["On the road", "[Meaning:] the designated road, the straight path, the very road that I needed. Similarly every ל', ב' and ה' when they are used as a prefix and are vocalized with a פַּתַּח refer to something specific that has already been mentioned elsewhere, or if it has been clear and obvious about which one he is speaking.", "בדרך. דרך המזומן, דרך הישר, באותו דרך שהייתי צריך. וכן כל בי\"ת ולמ\"ד וה\"א המשמשים בראש התיבה ונקודים בפת\"ח, מדברים בדבר הפשוט שנזכר כבר במקום אחר, או שהוא מבורר וניכר באיזו הוא מדבר:"]]}], [{"he": "וַתָּרָץ הַנַּעֲרָ וַתַּגֵּד לְבֵית אִמָּהּ כַּדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה", "en": "The girl ran and told her mother’s household of these these happenings.", "c": [["Her mother’s household", "It was customary for women to have a house in which to sit to do their work, and a daughter confides only in her mother.", "לבית אמה. דרך הנשים היתה, להיות להן בית לישב בו למלאכתן, ואין הבת מגדת אלא לאמה:"]]}], [{"he": "וּלְרִבְקָה אָח וּשְׁמוֹ לָבָן וַיָּרָץ לָבָן אֶל־הָאִישׁ הַחוּצָה אֶל־הָעָיִן", "en": "Rivkah had a brother whose name was Lavan, and Lavan ran outside to the man [standing] at the well.", "c": [["He ran", "Why did he [Lavan] run and for what did he run? “When he had seen the nose ring,” he said, “This one is rich” and made plans to get at his money.", "וירץ. למה רץ ועל מה רץ, ויהי כראות את הנזם, אמר, עשיר הוא זה, ונתן עיניו בממון:"]]}], [{"he": "וַיְהִי כִּרְאֹת אֶת־הַנֶּזֶם וְאֶת־הַצְּמִדִים עַל־יְדֵי אֲחֹתוֹ וּכְשָׁמְעוֹ אֶת־דִּבְרֵי רִבְקָה אֲחֹתוֹ לֵאמֹר כֹּה־דִבֶּר אֵלַי הָאִישׁ וַיָּבֹא אֶל־הָאִישׁ וְהִנֵּה עֹמֵד עַל־הַגְּמַלִּים עַל־הָעָיִן", "en": "When he had seen the nose ring and the bracelets on the hands of his sister, and heard the words of his sister, Rivkah saying, this is what the man spoke to me, that he [then] came to the man, who was still standing beside the camels at the well.", "c": [["Beside the camels", "To watch over them, as in “He stood over them,” [meaning:] in order to serve them.", "על הגמלים. לשמרן, כמו וְהוּא עוֹמֵד עֲלֵיהֶם (בראשית יח, ח) לשמשם:"]]}]];
const C3S24_LESSONS=[{"id": "cs24-1", "title": "Avraham's oath", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 24:1–9", "parts": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "phrases": [["וְאַבְרָהָם זָקֵן בָּא בַּיָּמִים וַה' בֵּרַךְ אֶת־אַבְרָהָם בַּכֹּל", "Avraham was old, advanced in days [years], and Adonoy had blessed Avraham in all things."], ["וַיֹּאמֶר אַבְרָהָם אֶל־עַבְדּוֹ זְקַן בֵּיתוֹ הַמֹּשֵׁל בְּכָל־אֲשֶׁר־לוֹ שִׂים־נָא יָדְךָ תַּחַת יְרֵכִי", "Avraham said to his servant, the senior [servant] of his household, who was in charge of all that he owned, Place your hand under my thigh."], ["וְאַשְׁבִּיעֲךָ בַּה' אֱלֹקֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם וֵאלֹקֵי הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר לֹא־תִקַּח אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי מִבְּנוֹת הַכְּנַעֲנִי אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי יוֹשֵׁב בְּקִרְבּוֹ", "I will have you swear by Adonoy, God of heaven and God of earth, that you will not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom I live."], ["כִּי אֶל־אַרְצִי וְאֶל־מוֹלַדְתִּי תֵּלֵךְ וְלָקַחְתָּ אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי לְיִצְחָק", "Instead, to my [native] land, to my birthplace, shall you go, and take a wife for my son, for Yitzchok,"], ["וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו הָעֶבֶד אוּלַי לֹא־תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרַי אֶל־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הֶהָשֵׁב אָשִׁיב אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־יָצָאתָ מִשָּׁם", "The servant said to him, Perhaps the woman will not want to come back with me to this land? Shall I bring your son back to the land from where you came?"], ["וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו אַבְרָהָם הִשָּׁמֶר לְךָ פֶּן־תָּשִׁיב אֶת־בְּנִי שָׁמָּה", "Avraham said to him, Take care, not to bring my son back there."], ["ה' אֱלֹקֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם אֲשֶׁר לְקָחַנִי מִבֵּית אָבִי וּמֵאֶרֶץ מוֹלַדְתִּי וַאֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר־לִי וַאֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע־לִי לֵאמֹר לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הוּא יִשְׁלַח מַלְאָכוֹ לְפָנֶיךָ וְלָקַחְתָּ אִשָּׁה לִבְנִי מִשָּׁם", "Adonoy, God of heaven, Who took me from my father’s house, and from the land of my birth, Who spoke to me, and Who swore to me, saying, To your descendants I will give this land—He will send His angel before you, and you shall take a wife for my son from there."], ["וְאִם־לֹא תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרֶיךָ וְנִקִּיתָ מִשְּׁבֻעָתִי זֹאת רַק אֶת־בְּנִי לֹא תָשֵׁב שָׁמָּה", "If the woman does not want to come back with you, you are absolved from this oath to me. But do not bring my son back there."], ["וַיָּשֶׂם הָעֶבֶד אֶת־יָדוֹ תַּחַת יֶרֶךְ אַבְרָהָם אֲדֹנָיו וַיִּשָּׁבַע לוֹ עַל־הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה", "The servant placed his hand under the thigh of Avraham, his master, and swore to him regarding this matter."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Rashi", "“Blessed Avraham in all things” — בַּכֹּל is numerically equal to בֵּן [son], and since he had a son he needed to find a wife for him."], "mref": 0}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "Avraham was old, advanced in days [years], and Adonoy had blessed Avraham in all things.", "tiles": ["וְאַבְרָהָם", "זָקֵן", "בָּא", "בַּיָּמִים"], "decoys": ["וְאִם־לֹא"], "id": "cs24-1-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How did Hashem bless Avraham?", "opts": ["With everything (בכל)", "Only with wealth", "Only with children", "Only with long life"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-1-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where did Avraham send his servant to find a wife for Yitzchak?", "opts": ["To Avraham's land and birthplace", "To Canaan", "To Mitzrayim", "To the Pelishtim"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-1-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 9, "note": ["Rashi", "“Adonoy, God of heaven Who took me from my father’s house” — Here he did not say “and the God of earth,” whereas, above he did say, “And I will have you swear, etc.” He, [Avraham] [in effect,] said to him [the servant], “Now He is the God of heaven and earth for I have made Him current on everyone’s tongue.”…"], "mref": 4}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Avraham allowed Yitzchak to leave Eretz Yisrael.", "a": false, "ex": "Avraham said: 'Take care, do not bring my son back there.'", "id": "cs24-1-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (24:5)", "before": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו הָעֶבֶד אוּלַי לֹא־תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרַי אֶל־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הֶהָשֵׁב אָשִׁיב אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־יָצָאתָ", "after": "", "opts": ["מִשָּׁם", "עִמָּכֶם", "עֶפְרוֹן"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו הָעֶבֶד אוּלַי לֹא־תֹאבֶה הָאִשָּׁה לָלֶכֶת אַחֲרַי אֶל־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת הֶהָשֵׁב אָשִׁיב אֶת־בִּנְךָ אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר־יָצָאתָ מִשָּׁם", "id": "cs24-1-5"}]}, {"id": "cs24-2", "title": "Eliezer sets out", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 24:10–14", "parts": [9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "phrases": [["וַיִּקַּח הָעֶבֶד עֲשָׂרָה גְמַלִּים מִגְּמַלֵּי אֲדֹנָיו וַיֵּלֶךְ וְכָל־טוּב אֲדֹנָיו בְּיָדוֹ וַיָּקָם וַיֵּלֶךְ אֶל־אֲרַם נַהֲרַיִם אֶל־עִיר נָחוֹר", "The servant took ten camels from his master’s camels and departed, and all the property of his master was in his hand. He rose and went to Aram Naharayim; to the city of Nachor."], ["וַיַּבְרֵךְ הַגְּמַלִּים מִחוּץ לָעִיר אֶל־בְּאֵר הַמָּיִם לְעֵת עֶרֶב לְעֵת צֵאת הַשֹּׁאֲבֹת", "He made the camels kneel outside the city, beside a well of water, in the evening, at the time the women go out to draw water."], ["וַיֹּאמַר ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם הַקְרֵה־נָא לְפָנַי הַיּוֹם וַעֲשֵׂה־חֶסֶד עִם אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם", "He said, Adonoy, God of my master, Avraham, be present before me today, and act kindly with my master, Avraham."], ["הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי נִצָּב עַל־עֵין הַמָּיִם וּבְנוֹת אַנְשֵׁי הָעִיר יֹצְאֹת לִשְׁאֹב מָיִם", "Behold, here I stand by this well of water, and the daughters of the townsmen are coming out to draw water."], ["וְהָיָה הַנַּעֲרָ אֲשֶׁר אֹמַר אֵלֶיהָ הַטִּי־נָא כַדֵּךְ וְאֶשְׁתֶּה וְאָמְרָה שְׁתֵה וְגַם־גְּמַלֶּיךָ אַשְׁקֶה אֹתָהּ הֹכַחְתָּ לְעַבְדְּךָ לְיִצְחָק וּבָהּ אֵדַע כִּי־עָשִׂיתָ חֶסֶד עִם־אֲדֹנִי", "Let it be that the girl to whom I say, Please, tip over your pitcher that I may drink and she will say Drink, and I will also give your camels to drink, will be the one whom You have determined for your servant, Yitzchok. With her I will know that You have dealt kindly with my master."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Rashi", "“From his master’s camels” — They were distinguishable from other camels, for they would go out only muzzled, out of concern for robbery that they not graze in others’ fields."], "mref": 9}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "The servant took ten camels from his master’s camels and departed, and all the property of…", "tiles": ["וַיִּקַּח", "הָעֶבֶד", "עֲשָׂרָה", "גְמַלִּים"], "decoys": ["הַשֹּׁאֲבֹת"], "id": "cs24-2-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "How many camels did Eliezer take?", "opts": ["Ten", "Two", "Seven", "Forty"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-2-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Where did Eliezer make the camels kneel?", "opts": ["By a well of water outside the city", "Inside the city", "At a river", "Near a tent"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-2-3"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What sign did Eliezer ask for?", "opts": ["The girl who offers water to him and to his camels", "The tallest girl", "The first girl to come", "A girl wearing gold"], "a": 0, "ex": "The sign shows kindness: she would give even the camels to drink.", "id": "cs24-2-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (24:12)", "before": "וַיֹּאמַר ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם הַקְרֵה־נָא לְפָנַי הַיּוֹם וַעֲשֵׂה־חֶסֶד עִם אֲדֹנִי", "after": "", "opts": ["אַבְרָהָם", "פֶּן־תָּשִׁיב", "מַרְאֶה"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַיֹּאמַר ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם הַקְרֵה־נָא לְפָנַי הַיּוֹם וַעֲשֵׂה־חֶסֶד עִם אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם", "id": "cs24-2-5"}]}, {"id": "cs24-3", "title": "At the well", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 24:15–21", "parts": [14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "phrases": [["וַיְהִי־הוּא טֶרֶם כִּלָּה לְדַבֵּר וְהִנֵּה רִבְקָה יֹצֵאת אֲשֶׁר יֻלְּדָה לִבְתוּאֵל בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֵשֶׁת נָחוֹר אֲחִי אַבְרָהָם וְכַדָּהּ עַל־שִׁכְמָהּ", "He had not yet finished speaking, and behold Rivkah came out. She had been born to Besu’eil, the son of Milkah, the wife of Nachor, Avraham’s brother. Her pitcher was on her shoulder."], ["וְהַנַּעֲרָ טֹבַת מַרְאֶה מְאֹד בְּתוּלָה וְאִישׁ לֹא יְדָעָהּ וַתֵּרֶד הָעַיְנָה וַתְּמַלֵּא כַדָּהּ וַתָּעַל", "The girl was very fine, and unmarried. She went down to the well, filled her pitcher, and came up."], ["וַיָּרָץ הָעֶבֶד לִקְרָאתָהּ וַיֹּאמֶר הַגְמִיאִינִי נָא מְעַט־מַיִם מִכַּדֵּךְ", "The servant ran toward her and said, Please let me sip a little water from your pitcher."], ["וַתֹּאמֶר שְׁתֵה אֲדֹנִי וַתְּמַהֵר וַתֹּרֶד כַּדָּהּ עַל־יָדָהּ וַתַּשְׁקֵהוּ", "She said, Drink, my master, and she quickly lowered her pitcher to her hand, and let him drink."], ["וַתְּכַל לְהַשְׁקֹתוֹ וַתֹּאמֶר גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ אֶשְׁאָב עַד אִם־כִּלּוּ לִשְׁתֹּת", "When she had finished giving him to drink, she said, I will also draw water for your camels, until they will have finished drinking."], ["וַתְּמַהֵר וַתְּעַר כַּדָּהּ אֶל־הַשֹּׁקֶת וַתָּרָץ עוֹד אֶל־הַבְּאֵר לִשְׁאֹב וַתִּשְׁאַב לְכָל־גְּמַלָּיו", "She quickly emptied her pitcher into the trough and she ran to the well again to draw water. and she drew water for all his camels."], ["וְהָאִישׁ מִשְׁתָּאֵה לָהּ מַחֲרִישׁ לָדַעַת הַהִצְלִיחַ ה' דַּרְכּוֹ אִם־לֹא", "The man, wondering at her, remained silent, waiting to determine whether Adonoy had made his mission successful, or not."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": null, "mref": 14}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "He had not yet finished speaking, and behold Rivkah came out. She had been born to Besu’ei…", "tiles": ["וַיְהִי־הוּא", "טֶרֶם", "כִּלָּה", "לְדַבֵּר"], "decoys": ["אִם־לֹא"], "id": "cs24-3-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did Rivkah offer after giving Eliezer water?", "opts": ["To draw water for all his camels", "To bring him bread", "To show him the way", "To call her father"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-3-2"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Rivkah came out before Eliezer finished his tefillah.", "a": true, "ex": "'He had not yet finished speaking, and behold Rivkah came out.'", "id": "cs24-3-3"}, {"t": "learn", "from": 4, "to": 7, "note": ["Rashi", "“Until they will have finished” — Here אִם is used to mean “that.” Onkelos translates it “they had enough” because that is the end of their drinking— when they have had enough to drink."], "mref": 18}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did Eliezer do while the camels drank?", "opts": ["He watched silently, waiting to see if Hashem made his way successful", "He went into the city", "He fed the camels himself", "He sang"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-3-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (24:19)", "before": "וַתְּכַל לְהַשְׁקֹתוֹ וַתֹּאמֶר גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ אֶשְׁאָב עַד אִם־כִּלּוּ", "after": "", "opts": ["לִשְׁתֹּת", "מֵאָה", "פֶּן־תָּשִׁיב"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַתְּכַל לְהַשְׁקֹתוֹ וַתֹּאמֶר גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ אֶשְׁאָב עַד אִם־כִּלּוּ לִשְׁתֹּת", "id": "cs24-3-5"}]}, {"id": "cs24-4", "title": "The gifts", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 24:22–25", "parts": [21, 22, 23, 24], "phrases": [["וַיְהִי כַּאֲשֶׁר כִּלּוּ הַגְּמַלִּים לִשְׁתּוֹת וַיִּקַּח הָאִישׁ נֶזֶם זָהָב בֶּקַע מִשְׁקָלוֹ וּשְׁנֵי צְמִידִים עַל־יָדֶיהָ עֲשָׂרָה זָהָב מִשְׁקָלָם", "When the camels had finished drinking, the man took a gold nose ring, weighing half a shekel, and two bracelets for her arms, weighing ten gold shekel."], ["וַיֹּאמֶר בַּת־מִי אַתְּ הַגִּידִי נָא לִי הֲיֵשׁ בֵּית־אָבִיךְ מָקוֹם לָנוּ לָלִין", "He said to her, Whose daughter are you? Please tell me. Is there place in your father’s house for us to spend the night."], ["וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו בַּת־בְּתוּאֵל אָנֹכִי בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה לְנָחוֹר", "She said to him, I am the daughter of Besueil, the son of Milkah, whom she bore to Nachor."], ["וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו גַּם־תֶּבֶן גַּם־מִסְפּוֹא רַב עִמָּנוּ גַּם־מָקוֹם לָלוּן", "She said to him, We have plenty of straw and fodder, and also a place to spend the night."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 4, "note": ["Rashi", "“Half a shekel” — This is symbolic of the shekels of Israel [which were] a בֶקַע [half-shekel] per head."], "mref": 21}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "When the camels had finished drinking, the man took a gold nose ring, weighing half a shek…", "tiles": ["וַיְהִי", "כַּאֲשֶׁר", "כִּלּוּ", "הַגְּמַלִּים"], "decoys": ["הֲיֵשׁ"], "id": "cs24-4-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did Eliezer give?", "opts": ["A gold nose ring and two bracelets", "Silver coins", "A camel", "A new garment"], "a": 0, "ex": "Rashi: the two bracelets hint at the two Luchos, and their ten shekel at the Ten Commandments.", "id": "cs24-4-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Whose daughter was Rivkah?", "opts": ["Besuel, son of Nachor", "Lavan", "Ephron", "Lot"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-4-3"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Rivkah said there was room for them to spend the night.", "a": true, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-4-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (24:24)", "before": "וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו בַּת־בְּתוּאֵל אָנֹכִי בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה", "after": "", "opts": ["לְנָחוֹר", "אִשָּׁה", "יָדְךָ"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַתֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו בַּת־בְּתוּאֵל אָנֹכִי בֶּן־מִלְכָּה אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה לְנָחוֹר", "id": "cs24-4-5"}]}, {"id": "cs24-5", "title": "Baruch Hashem", "short": "Chayei Sarah · 24:26–30", "parts": [25, 26, 27, 28, 29], "phrases": [["וַיִּקֹּד הָאִישׁ וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ לַה'", "The man bowed [his head] and prostrated himself to Adonoy."], ["וַיֹּאמֶר בָּרוּךְ ה' אֱלֹקֵי אֲדֹנִי אַבְרָהָם אֲשֶׁר לֹא־עָזַב חַסְדּוֹ וַאֲמִתּוֹ מֵעִם אֲדֹנִי אָנֹכִי בַּדֶּרֶךְ נָחַנִי ה' בֵּית אֲחֵי אֲדֹנִי", "He said, Blessed is Adonoy, God of my master, Avraham, Who has not abandoned His kindness and truth [in dealing] with my master. I am still on the road and Adonoy has led me to the house of my master’s brethren."], ["וַתָּרָץ הַנַּעֲרָ וַתַּגֵּד לְבֵית אִמָּהּ כַּדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה", "The girl ran and told her mother’s household of these these happenings."], ["וּלְרִבְקָה אָח וּשְׁמוֹ לָבָן וַיָּרָץ לָבָן אֶל־הָאִישׁ הַחוּצָה אֶל־הָעָיִן", "Rivkah had a brother whose name was Lavan, and Lavan ran outside to the man [standing] at the well."], ["וַיְהִי כִּרְאֹת אֶת־הַנֶּזֶם וְאֶת־הַצְּמִדִים עַל־יְדֵי אֲחֹתוֹ וּכְשָׁמְעוֹ אֶת־דִּבְרֵי רִבְקָה אֲחֹתוֹ לֵאמֹר כֹּה־דִבֶּר אֵלַי הָאִישׁ וַיָּבֹא אֶל־הָאִישׁ וְהִנֵּה עֹמֵד עַל־הַגְּמַלִּים עַל־הָעָיִן", "When he had seen the nose ring and the bracelets on the hands of his sister, and heard the words of his sister, Rivkah saying, this is what the man spoke to me, that he [then] came to the man, who was still standing beside the camels at the well."]], "steps": [{"t": "learn", "from": 0, "to": 5, "note": ["Rashi", "“On the road” — [Meaning:] the designated road, the straight path, the very road that I needed. Similarly every ל', ב' and ה' when they are used as a prefix and are vocalized with a פַּתַּח refer to something specific that has already been mentioned elsewhere, or…"], "mref": 25}, {"t": "order", "q": "Build the start of the pasuk", "en": "The man bowed [his head] and prostrated himself to Adonoy.", "tiles": ["וַיִּקֹּד", "הָאִישׁ", "וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ", "לַה'"], "decoys": ["אֲדֹנִי"], "id": "cs24-5-1"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "What did Eliezer do when he heard the answer?", "opts": ["He bowed and thanked Hashem", "He ran home", "He gave more gifts", "He asked for food"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-5-2"}, {"t": "mc", "q": "Who was Rivkah's brother?", "opts": ["Lavan", "Besuel", "Nachor", "Eliezer"], "a": 0, "ex": "", "id": "cs24-5-3"}, {"t": "tf", "q": "Lavan ran out to Eliezer after he saw the jewelry.", "a": true, "ex": "Rashi: he saw the gold and set his eyes on the money.", "id": "cs24-5-4"}, {"t": "fill", "q": "Complete the pasuk (24:28)", "before": "וַתָּרָץ הַנַּעֲרָ וַתַּגֵּד לְבֵית אִמָּהּ כַּדְּבָרִים", "after": "", "opts": ["הָאֵלֶּה", "בְּנֵי־חֵת", "עַל־פְּנֵי"], "a": 0, "ex": "וַתָּרָץ הַנַּעֲרָ וַתַּגֵּד לְבֵית אִמָּהּ כַּדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה", "id": "cs24-5-5"}]}];
